      exp: 'In Necochea, Argentina, investigators used a fingerprint to identify the culprit in the 1892 Francisca Rojas case, relying on Juan Vucetich’s system developed in La Plata.',
      sig: 'Argentina became the first country to rely on fingerprints as its main method of criminal identification.',
      fact: 'Vucetich’s “dactyloscopy” system became the basis of fingerprint classification across much of the Spanish-speaking world.',
      nuance: 'Fingerprint science also developed in British India (the Henry system) and Britain (Galton).',
